# Usar con la extensión "REST Client" de VS Code (o copiar como curl)
@base = http://localhost:3000/api
@email = ana@test.com
@password = supersecreta

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Health de la base de datos
GET {{base}}/health/db

### Listar tareas sin token (401)
GET {{base}}/tasks

### Registrar usuario (201; si se repite da 409)
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Login con contraseña incorrecta (401)
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "incorrecta" }

### Login (200): el token queda en la variable token
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Usuario actual
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Listar tareas (autenticado)
GET {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Obtener una tarea
GET {{base}}/tasks/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Crear tarea
POST {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Preparar la demo", "description": "Ensayar cada paso" }

### Crear tarea inválida (400)
POST {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "" }

### Marcar como hecha
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "done": true }

### Actualizar sin campos (400)
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Id inválido (400)
GET {{base}}/tasks/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Eliminar (204; si se repite da 404)
DELETE {{base}}/tasks/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
